From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the kept-store stamp can leave out the two switches that only decide when work happens (waveydude's 0926, EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SKIP_RUNTIME), off by default

What: the kept translations (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP) are stamped with NAME=VALUE of every set switch
in TranslationSwitches. EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT (a refused ASTC decode waits for its image's next
use, vk_texture_cache.cpp) and EDEN_NX2_PRELOAD_ALL_PIPELINES (which kept pipelines the boot builds,
vk_pipeline_cache.cpp) are in that list but change no translation: setting, clearing or changing
either one starts an empty store and a long first boot (his: 635 s for 4,681 pipelines).

With EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SKIP_RUNTIME=1 (exact "1") the stamp's switch part is made again without
those two names (SwitchHashWithoutRuntime, the same FNV-1a loop with a skip), so flipping either
keeps the store, and one INFO line says so once. The two names stay in the list (the switch-list
check wants every name the video core reads there); the new switch is an EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_ name,
which the list never holds. It applies to both stamps (the kept store and the shader set).

Off (unset or anything but "1"): MakeStamp's loop and string are untouched, so the stamp is byte
for byte T147's; the recount is not made and nothing is logged. Our play settings set
EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT=1, so an unconditional 0926 would have moved his stamp (switches 42 ->
41); off it stays 42:6af20c62bf018ae2 (t149/check/host149). Turning the switch on is one stamp
change, so one cold boot; doing it with a new install costs nothing extra (the eboot field of the
stamp changes on every install anyway).

Placement: the recount is a helper after SwitchNumber and a block after MakeStamp's loop, away from
the lines T138's EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SOURCE_STAMP (0596) changes: T138's 0594-0596 still apply on
top of this unchanged. With both on they skip the same two names.

Origin and credit: waveydude, patch 0926 ("Keep switches that do not change a translation out of
the kept-store stamp"), commit 07a1fb0; his skip list and comments, put behind a switch here.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
index 663bac2..78a0485 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_prep.cpp
@@ -16,7 +16,9 @@
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <string_view>
 #include <system_error>
+#include <tuple>
 #include <type_traits>
+#include <utility>
 
 #include <fmt/format.h>
 
@@ -193,6 +195,48 @@ constexpr const char* TranslationSwitches[] = {
     return end == value || number == 0 ? fallback : static_cast<size_t>(number);
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SKIP_RUNTIME=1 (exact "1"; waveydude's 0926): switches the list above names
+// (it holds every switch the video core reads) that decide when work happens and never what a
+// shader is translated to. With the switch on they stay out of the stamp, set or not, so turning
+// one on or off keeps the store. Off (unset or anything but "1"): the stamp is as before. The
+// switch itself is not in the list (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_ names never are).
+constexpr std::string_view NotTranslation[]{
+    "EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT",        // a refused ASTC decode waits for its image's next use
+    "EDEN_NX2_PRELOAD_ALL_PIPELINES", // which kept pipelines the boot builds
+};
+
+[[nodiscard]] bool SkipRuntimeSwitches() {
+    static const bool skip = SwitchIs("EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SKIP_RUNTIME", '1');
+    return skip;
+}
+
+/// The stamp's switch part (how many are set, FNV-1a over NAME=VALUE\n of each, in list order)
+/// without the NotTranslation names: the same loop as MakeStamp's, which it replaces when
+/// SkipRuntimeSwitches() is on.
+[[nodiscard]] std::pair<u32, u64> SwitchHashWithoutRuntime() {
+    u64 hash = 0xcbf29ce484222325ULL;
+    const auto mix = [&hash](std::string_view text) {
+        for (const char c : text) {
+            hash = (hash ^ static_cast<u8>(c)) * 0x100000001b3ULL;
+        }
+    };
+    u32 set = 0;
+    for (const char* const name : TranslationSwitches) {
+        if (std::ranges::find(NotTranslation, std::string_view{name}) !=
+            std::end(NotTranslation)) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        if (const char* const value = std::getenv(name)) {
+            mix(name);
+            mix("=");
+            mix(value);
+            mix("\n");
+            ++set;
+        }
+    }
+    return {set, hash};
+}
+
 /// Which build runs: the size and write time of the app's eboot (the folders the PS5 app looks
 /// for itself in, headless/storage_paths.h; EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_EXE names another file). A build
 /// that is installed again gets a new store even when it translates the same: it costs one
@@ -893,6 +937,18 @@ std::string MakeStamp(u32 cache_version, u32 driver_id, u32 driver_version,
             ++set;
         }
     }
+    // EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SKIP_RUNTIME=1: the switch part again without the switches that only
+    // decide when work happens (kept apart from the loop above so it stays as it was when off).
+    if (SkipRuntimeSwitches()) {
+        std::tie(set, hash) = SwitchHashWithoutRuntime();
+        static const bool said = [] {
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                     "EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SKIP_RUNTIME: EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT and "
+                     "EDEN_NX2_PRELOAD_ALL_PIPELINES are left out of the kept-store stamp");
+            return true;
+        }();
+        static_cast<void>(said);
+    }
     // The settings the translation reads (shader_recompiler: rescaling_pass.cpp,
     // translate_program.cpp, emit_spirv.cpp, emit_spirv_image.cpp). A switch or setting that is
     // missed here is still noticed by the comparison at boot when it changes a compared pipeline.
